Implement task page window for integration batch 1. Input is {items:array,page:integer,pageSize:positive integer}. Pages are one-based. Return a new array containing exactly the requested page; page<1 or beyond the end returns [].
Export JavaScript function solve(input), with no dependencies. Do not mutate input. Return only the implementation.
Repair this faulty implementation to satisfy the contract: export const solve=({items,page,pageSize})=>items.slice(page*pageSize,page*pageSize+pageSize);

Implement task async result collection for integration batch 1. Input is an array of finite numbers. solve must return a Promise resolving to a new array of doubled values in original order. Each transformation must await Promise.resolve(value*2); do not return before those transformations finish.
Export JavaScript function solve(input), with no dependencies. Do not mutate input. Return only the implementation.
Repair this faulty implementation to satisfy the contract: export async function solve(items){const result=[];items.forEach(async v=>{result.push(await Promise.resolve(v*2));});return [...result];}

